This project draws on ideas and checklist items from the following
MIT-licensed projects. No source code is copied; where wording is
adapted, the source is named in the file that uses it.

- Checklist Design skills (https://github.com/Checklist-Design/skills)
  audit statuses (present / partial / missing / not needed / can't tell),
  strengths-first critique convention.
- mobile-screen-eval (https://github.com/jainulabudeenm/mobile-screen-eval)
  three-layer evaluation (Nielsen heuristics, WCAG 2.1 AA, mobile
  platform accessibility), 0-4 severity scale, batch report layout.
- design-skills by parhamb (https://github.com/parhamb/design-skills)
  navigation and visual-design checklist items.
- appllama-skills (https://github.com/Appllama/appllama-skills)
  navigation semantics (push vs replace, sheet vs page, no-back screens).

- Nielsen Norman Group, "10 Usability Heuristics for User Interface
  Design" (https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ten-usability-heuristics/):
  the heuristic sweep in skills/cerebro-audit/references/heuristics.md.
- impeccable (https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable, Apache-2.0) and
  klamben (https://github.com/obiwancenobi/klamben, Apache-2.0):
  anti-pattern ideas in skills/cerebro-design/references/anti-patterns.md.

The capture harness follows the image-capture pattern used by
flutter_test (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors).
